  "slug": "spin-altermagnetism-d7e3",
  "summary": "Eight preprints link altermagnetic, odd-parity and spin-nematic order to concrete probes: magneto-optics, spin photocurrent, charge-spin transport and thermal Hall.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is theory that connects measurable responses to the symmetry of unconventional magnetic order. For altermagnets, noncoplanar antiferromagnets and odd-parity magnets, the proposed probes are octupolar magneto-optical effects, nonlinear spin generation and spin photocurrent, and charge-spin selection rules with temporal-spectral separation in transport. Twist engineering of collinear bilayers is proposed to yield quasicrystalline altermagnets with high-order spin polarization. On the magnon side, single magnons and bound magnon pairs in pyrochlore spin-nematics give competing thermal Hall contributions, allowing field-tunable sign reversal. In CrI3 nanotubes, an axial field produces a conical phase and a large pseudo-orbital magnon moment. In BiFeO3, gate-controlled domain boundaries modulate nonreciprocal magnons in a proposed transistor. Cavity photon condensation driven by scalar spin chirality is more peripheral. All eight are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
